  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nWhile it will not rain continuously, showers are expected from \nFriday through a good portion of Saturday across many portions of \nIowa with peals of thunder likely on Friday as well. There is \nvariability in the models whether this rain will last all the \nway through Saturday or if Saturday starts to turn drier or if \nSunday morning will have lingering showers as well. Regardless, \ntrick or treaters will encounter mild conditions and perhaps \ndamp ones as well Friday or Saturday evening depending on when\nthe festivities are held. Quickly following this southern \nstream wave will be a more pronounced mid-level trough or closed\nlow that will push over the Rockies by the start of next week\nand into the central part of the country by the middle of next \nweek. While there is uncertainty in the exact mid-level pattern\nevolution early next week, confidence is increasing in another \nround of showers and thunderstorms in this timeframe. With this \nbeing one of several rounds of rainfall spread out over the next\nweek with total rainfall between 1.5 and 2.5 inches over the \nstate from the grand ensemble, some within bank rises are\npossible on mainly smaller streams and tributaries to the larger\nrivers according to recent runs of the National Water Model \nforced by the NBM and GFS.",
